# Embedded medical firmware coding (from FW_Req_Doc_CPAP)

Full doc: `FW_Req_Doc_CPAP/Embedded_C_CPP_Coding_Guidelines_Medical_Device.docx`

## P1 — mandatory
- Fixed-width types (`uint8_t`, `int32_t`); no plain `int` where size matters.
- **No malloc/free/new/delete** on safety-critical runtime paths after init.
- **Bounds-check** all buffer/index access (USB, BLE, NVM, sensors).
- Initialize locals; no recursion; no UB (signed overflow, bad shifts).
- Check all HAL/driver return values or document conscious ignore.
- ISR-shared data: `volatile` + critical section/queue/mutex as needed.
- Bounded waits with timeout; watchdog-safe loops; **fail-safe defaults**.
- Hardware access only in driver/BSP; app logic uses module APIs.
- Units in names: `pressure_cmh2o`, `timeout_ms`, `flow_slm`.

## P2 — required style (match existing CPAP_InitialCode)
- `module_action()` public functions; `static` file-private helpers.
- `g_` globals (debugger-tunable where useful); `s_` file-static state.
- Accepted legacy module prefixes: `Therapy_`, `Apap_`, `BlowerCtrl_`, `AMS5935_` — use for new APIs in those modules; prefer `g_` + unit suffix for debugger globals.
- 4 spaces, braces on all control blocks, no magic numbers, no dead/commented code.
- One purpose per function; nesting ≤3; DRY; comments explain **why** and units.
- C++ (TouchGFX): controlled subset — no exceptions/RTTI in RT paths; simple init; `const` correctness.

## Medical process hooks
- Risk-control code identifiable in design + tests.
- NVM settings: CRC, versioning, range checks before use.
- Static analysis + peer review for production changes.
